{"name":"J’s Big Heart","hex":"#a06856","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"big","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Biangai."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of great size, large.","Fat."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/big"},{"term":"heart","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A muscular organ that pumps blood through the body, traditionally thought to be the seat of emotion.","One's feelings and emotions, especially considered as part of one's character."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To be fond of. Often bracketed or abbreviated with a heart symbol. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","To mark a comment, post, reply, etc., with the heart symbol (❤)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heart"}],"entries":[{"title":"Big Heart","blocks":[{"text":"\"Big Heart\" is a debut song recorded by American country music group Gibson/Miller Band. It was released in November 1992 as the first single from the album Where There's Smoke.... The song reached #37 on the Billboard Hot Country Songs & Tracks chart. The song was written by group members Dave Gibson and Blue Miller, along with Freddy Weller."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_Heart","wikidata":"Q28449549"},{"title":"Heart","blocks":[{"text":"The heart is a muscular organ found in humans and other animals. This organ pumps blood through the blood vessels. The heart and blood vessels together make up the circulatory system. The pumped blood carries oxygen and nutrients to the tissue, while carrying metabolic waste such as carbon dioxide to the lungs. In humans, the heart is approximately the size of a closed fist and is located between the lungs, in the middle compartment of the chest, called the mediastinum."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Heart_anterior_exterior_view.png/330px-Heart_anterior_exterior_view.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heart","wikidata":"Q1072"},{"title":"J","blocks":[{"text":"J is the tenth letter of the Latin alphabet, used in the modern English alphabet, the alphabets of other Western European languages and others worldwide. Its usual name in English is jay, with a now-uncommon variant jye."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Latin_letter_J.svg/330px-Latin_letter_J.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/J","wikidata":"Q9773"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b7/Humhrt2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b7/Humhrt2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Human heart during an autopsy","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHumhrt2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/CG_Heart.gif/500px-CG_Heart.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/CG_Heart.gif/500px-CG_Heart.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Computer-generated animation of a beating human heart","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACG_Heart.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Heart_near.png/500px-Heart_near.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Heart_near.png/500px-Heart_near.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The human heart is in the middle of the thorax, with its apex pointing to the left.[14]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHeart_near.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb